{
  "adjustments": [
    {
      "target": "u1",
      "focus": ["S", "C"],
      "change": "Retain the single-object anti-repetition and coverage search discipline, but make it operable under the Actor's recent-history protocol: choose a different candidate location from the recent visible history; cover candidate container/surface types not among those just checked, including opening closed cabinets/drawers and checking shelves/basins; and explicitly preserve returning to a required transformation site or the named target receptacle after the needed object has been acquired.",
      "reason": "Current single-object clean tasks show the failure mode: after taking the wrong `knife 1` at `P7:5`, the run placed it at `P7:9` and then cycled drawers/countertops without finding a butterknife (`P7:14`, `P7:50`, `P7:outcome`); `P8` cycled cabinets/surfaces and never found the soapbar (`P8:34`, `P8:50`, `P8:outcome`). Successful runs show required post-acquisition returns: `P6:4`-`P6:6` and `P9:4`-`P9:5` return to sinkbasin to clean, and `P10:12`-`P10:15` uses fridge then microwave. Grounding applicability in recent visible history and adding the preservation boundary avoids blocking those productive returns while still addressing the cycling defect; the local grounding is an unverified scope choice that trades global completeness for protocol-usable detection.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n - If recent observations show you just visited, opened, or toggled a candidate location and it did not reveal the needed object, choose a different candidate location instead of returning to it.\n-- Cover candidate container and surface types you have not yet checked in the current scene, including opening closed cabinets and drawers and checking shelves and other receptacles, rather than cycling through the same small subset of locations.\n-- If you detect you have returned to an already-checked location without new progress, break the loop by going to a still-unvisited candidate location.\n+- Cover candidate container and surface types that are not among those just checked, including opening closed cabinets and drawers and checking shelves and other receptacles, rather than cycling through the same small subset of locations.\n+- If the recent visible history shows you have returned to an already-checked location without new progress, break the loop by going to a different candidate location.\n+- Once the needed object has been acquired, returning to a required transformation site (such as sinkbasin 1, fridge 1, or microwave 1) or to the named target receptacle to complete cleaning, cooling, heating, or placement is productive and must not be blocked by this anti-revisit guidance.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "u2",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "`P7:5` took `knife 1` when the task required a butterknife, then `P7:7` cleaned it and `P7:9` placed it without completing the task and without finding the named type; `P6:3` shows the supported exact-type acquisition followed by clean/place. The exact-type requirement and the resume-search condition directly address that observed defect, including the post-placement search failure in `P7` (`P7:14`, `P7:50`). No supplied response shows the exact-type requirement or the resume-search condition obstructing the successful clean/cool/place patterns in `P6`, `P9`, or `P10`, and the search-discipline coordination is handled in `u1`.",
      "to": null
    }
  ],
